==Venue==
[[File:StadeFranceNationsLeague2018.jpg|thumb|275px|The [[Stade de France]] in [[Saint-Denis, Seine-Saint-Denis|Saint-Denis]] hosted the final.]]

The final was originally awarded to the [[Allianz Arena]] in Munich, Germany.<ref name="hosts announced"/> When the [[Impact of the COVID-19 pandemic on association football|COVID-19 pandemic]] forced the [[2020 UEFA Champions League final|2020 final]] to be relocated from the [[Atatürk Olympic Stadium]] in Istanbul to the [[Estádio da Luz]] in Lisbon, the Allianz Arena was reawarded with the [[2023 UEFA Champions League final|2023 final]] and the 2022 final was given to the original host of the [[2021 UEFA Champions League final|2021 final]], the [[Krestovsky Stadium]] in [[Saint Petersburg]].<ref name="ExCo 17 June"/>

Following the [[2022 Russian invasion of Ukraine|Russian invasion of Ukraine]] in February 2022, [[UEFA]] organised an emergency meeting of its executive committee on 25 February, at which it decided to move the final to the [[Stade de France]] in [[Saint-Denis, Seine-Saint-Denis|Saint-Denis]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.uefa.com/news-media/news/0272-148740475a92-1b97baa3e9d7-1000--decisions-from-today-s-extraordinary-uefa-executive-committee-m/ |title=Decisions from today's extraordinary UEFA Executive Committee meeting |work=UEFA.com |year=2022 | access-date=25 February 2022}}</ref> Other cities proposed as replacement hosts were [[Amsterdam]], [[Barcelona]], [[Munich]] and [[Rome]].<ref name="rsport">{{cite news |title=УЕФА лишил Петербург финала Лиги чемпионов: подробности |url=https://rsport.ria.ru/20220225/futbol-1774686959.html |publisher=[[RIA Novosti]] |date=25 February 2022 |access-date=25 February 2022 |language=ru |trans-title=UEFA deprived St. Petersburg of the Champions League final: details}}</ref> This was the first UEFA Champions League final to take place in France since [[2006 UEFA Champions League final|2006]], where [[FC Barcelona|Barcelona]] secured their second title by defeating [[Arsenal F.C.|Arsenal]] 2–1.<ref name="rsport"/>

===Host selection===
{{for|the details on the selection of Munich as the original host for the final|2023 UEFA Champions League final#Host selection}}

An open bidding process was launched on 28 September 2018 by UEFA to select the venues of the finals of the UEFA Champions League, UEFA Europa League, and UEFA Women's Champions League in 2021. Associations had until 26 October 2018 to express interest, and bid dossiers must be submitted by 15 February 2019. UEFA announced on 1 November 2018 that two associations had expressed interest in hosting the 2021 UEFA Champions League final,<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.uefa.com/news-media/news/0250-0c5119fbc7e9-b9de0907b594-1000--11-associations-interested-in-hosting-2021-club-finals/ |title=11 associations interested in hosting 2021 club finals |work=UEFA.com |date=1 November 2018}}</ref> and on 22 February 2019 that both associations submitted their dossiers by the deadline.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.uefa.com/news-media/news/024e-0f8e68aa43f5-6b3adef08395-1000--9-associations-bidding-to-host-2021-club-finals/ |title=9 associations bidding to host 2021 club finals |work=UEFA.com |date=22 February 2019}}</ref>

